<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Josef Friedrich Matthes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1886">1886</a>–<a href="/years/1943">1943</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Josef Friedrich Matthes was a German journalist and Rhenish separatist who led the provisional government of the Rhenish Republic in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koblenz">Koblenz</a> in 1923, alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hans-adam-dorten">Hans Adam Dorten</a>. The republic depended on the tolerance of French occupation forces and collapsed within months. Matthes went into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, and his citizenship was later revoked by the Nazi regime.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/josef-friedrich-matthes.jpg" alt="Josef Friedrich Matthes" width="320" height="540" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bain News Service, publisher. Photo originally taken by Karl Albert Zimmermann (1885-1943), Lindstedt &amp; Zimmerman... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Matthes_5375079625_19c03f8c10_o.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
